Transpose then reverse each row. O(n^2) for nxn.

```python
def rotate_matrix(m):
    n = len(m)
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(i + 1, n):
            m[i][j], m[j][i] = m[j][i], m[i][j]
    for row in m:
        row.reverse()
    return m
```

